From af5beefb7440500194b67a0b5878dbca042d6483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:24:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0021: name the cause of a takeover timeout, do not guess it

0020 prints one sentence for every miss: "its personality did not match this
card's device id". On a recovery boot that sentence is false - Apple's
AMDRadeonX6000 kext is not loaded there, so no personality of Apple's could
have matched anything, and the owner would chase a device-id spoof that cannot
help. A timeout has three causes and each one has a different fix.

accel_takeover_diagnosis() turns the miss into one of them: the accelerator
class is not registered on this boot (recovery, or the kext is missing), the
accelerator attached but its start() failed before announcing itself, or the
kext is loaded and nothing attached to the card - only the last one is about
the device id.

Two facts are gathered after the wait, not at arm time, so a kext that loads
late still counts: whether AMDRadeonX6000_AMDNavi21GraphicsAccelerator is a
registered class (OSMetaClass::getMetaClassWithName - libkern/OSKext.h is not
in MacKernelSDK), and whether any child of the card's provider is a class whose
name contains "Accelerator". takeover_arm() therefore takes the IOPCIDevice the
fire block already holds, and the report prints both bits so a photograph can
be read without a terminal.

The headline for TimedOut stops asserting the id and points at the cause line.
Host suite 89 checks / 0 failures, plant suite 41/41 caught, 0 escaped.
